    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1431">

                <pb facs="0940" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/369.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that it appears from a telegram I have just received from the
                    Minister of Spain in Mexico that the Constitutionalists at Zacatecas have shot
                    three priests and expelled about twenty. Senor Cologan adds that several Sisters
                    of St. Therese are in hiding at that place.</p>
                <p>I beg your excellency kindly to take an interest in the fate of those unfortunate
                    people and commend to your attention more particularly the Sisters of St.
                    Therese of whom several are Spanish.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
